## The Company They Keep
{{ warband }}
- You don't know who these fighters are or where they came from. All you have is what your eyes tell you: armed, easy about it, and following one person's lead.
- Let it weigh on you the way it would weigh on anyone. Most folk get careful around that much steel — softer voice, fairer price, shorter argument. A guard stays civil but starts counting heads. Someone bold might still push their luck; they just know exactly what they are pushing against.
- Nothing about them says rampage — no drawn weapons, no threats. It is the quiet kind of dangerous, and quiet is worse.
